{
  "overall_diagnosis": "Build failures in fix-build-google-auto are primarily due to Maven dependency and plugin resolution/execution problems under legacy CI/JDK constraints (notably TLS/SSL transport failures to Maven Central and ensuing missing classes from unresolved artifacts). Secondary issues involve multi-module reactor behavior and non-ideal ordering/mixing of lifecycle phases and plugin goals (e.g., go-offline/test/clean), which can mask root causes and cascade failures across modules. The skill gaps are mostly around practical troubleshooting for legacy environments (JDK7/old Maven), repository/protocol configuration, and concrete plugin/dependency repair techniques (pinning versions, exclusions, and safe temporary skips).",
