    {
      "path": "maven-plugin-configuration/SKILL.md",
      "confidence": 0.86,
      "diagnosis": "Evidence repeatedly shows Maven plugin resolution and plugin execution failures (dependency:go-offline/resolve-plugins, enforcer, surefire, invoker, compiler/annotation processing). The skill mentions pluginRepositories but lacks actionable troubleshooting for plugin resolution vs dependency resolution, legacy TLS/JDK compatibility, pinning compatible plugin versions, and handling plugin classpath/transitive dependency issues that can surface as NoClassDefFoundError during build steps.",
      "repair_instruction": "Add a focused troubleshooting section covering: (1) differentiating pluginRepositories vs repositories and when to use settings.xml mirrors vs POM changes; (2) diagnosing plugin transfer/TLS failures in legacy environments (e.g., old JDKs/Maven) including repository URL/protocol checks and when environment flags/settings are required; (3) overriding/pinning plugin versions via <pluginManagement> for JDK compatibility; (4) excluding/overriding problematic transitive plugin dependencies when plugin classpath failures occur; (5) CI-stability controls for common plugins (surefire/invoker/enforcer) including safe, profile-guarded skips (e.g., -DskipTests, enforcer.skip, invoker.skip) and criteria for when temporary skips are acceptable. Include concrete POM snippets for pluginManagement overrides and profile-based executions."
    },
    {
      "path": "maven-dependency-management/SKILL.md",
      "confidence": 0.83,
      "diagnosis": "Failures include dependency descriptor transfer errors (TLS/SSL) and downstream compilation/runtime missing-class symptoms (e.g., NoClassDefFoundError for auto-common/MoreElements) consistent with unresolved or misaligned transitive dependencies. The skill covers basic dependency declaration but lacks practical guidance for diagnosing resolution failures in constrained/legacy CI, fixing transitive dependency mismatches, and applying cross-JDK compatibility shims (adding/replacing JDK-removed artifacts, excluding obsolete deps) commonly needed in these builds.",
      "repair_instruction": "Add practical troubleshooting guidance for: (1) repository transport/TLS resolution failures (how to confirm what failed with -X/-U and dependency:tree/resolve, and when to use mirrors/settings vs POM); (2) interpreting missing-class errors as dependency graph problems and fixing them with explicit deps, exclusions, and version alignment; (3) using <dependencyManagement> to force consistent versions across multi-module projects; (4) cross-JDK compatibility patterns (replacing removed JDK-provided artifacts, adding javax/jakarta annotation APIs when needed, excluding obsolete tools.jar-era deps). Provide examples for dependency:tree-driven diagnosis, an exclusion snippet, and a dependencyManagement alignment snippet."
    },
    {
      "path": "maven-build-lifecycle/SKILL.md",
      "confidence": 0.62,
      "diagnosis": "Command usage and logs indicate confusion/fragility around mixing lifecycle phases with plugin goals and multi-module reactor behavior (e.g., go-offline/test/clean ordering, verify vs install impacts, reactor cascades and banned modules). The skill is largely a phase list and lacks pragmatic guidance for diagnosing reactor failures, resuming builds, and choosing correct phase/goal sequences for CI, especially in multi-module projects with integration-test/invoker steps.",
      "repair_instruction": "Add a lifecycle debugging subsection: explain why clean should typically precede compile/test and how mixing plugin goals (e.g., dependency:go-offline) with phases affects outcomes; provide recommended CI command patterns (e.g., go-offline before build, then clean verify/install as appropriate). Include multi-module reactor troubleshooting: reading the reactor summary, isolating modules with -pl/-am, resuming with -rf, and understanding how early-module failures cause downstream skips/bans (and when install is required for modules/tests that expect artifacts in the local repo)."
